858c1a9b-69e1-4fe3-82b1-ae8731f7a394	[Context: cbc > esr | mayo]\nMany conditions can affect the properties of blood and change how quickly red blood cells sink in a sample of blood. Conditions that can affect the sed rate include:\n\nAdvanced age.\nAnemia.\nPregnancy.\nKidney problems.\nThyroid disease.\nSome cancers, such as multiple myeloma.\nInfection.\nInjury.\n\nYour health care team will consider any other conditions you have when reviewing your sed rate test results. Talk to your rheumatologist or health care specialist about what your sed rate results mean and ask them any questions you may have.\n\nOct. 15, 2025	{"url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/sed-rate/about/pac-20384797", "title": "ESR (Erythrocyte Sedimentation Rate)", "topic": "esr", "source": "Mayo Clinic", "category": "cbc", "file_path": "cbc/esr/clean/mayo/v1.md", "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_org_code": "mayo", "parent_document_id": "4e11da53-aa63-47e0-b29e-0ea2d0bdfb12"}	[0.024453072,-0.0011048064,-0.014908808,-0.054365065,0.0029333024,-0.012691912,0.005739416,0.024131944,0.02241964,0.02166939,-0.008361468,-0.0090118935,-0.018944338,0.022628644,0.11268677,-0.009486272,-0.00035842785,0.010811058,0.012428505,0.011496735,0.0065003047,0.005457415,-0.0069156075,-0.010743867,0.007837482,-0.0042027007,-0.010605217,-0.042342506,0.047580812,-0.007510796,0.009413765,-0.016874714,0.010437486,0.027674412,-0.0013235054,0.033176344,-0.0073099914,-0.0049149473,-0.00017319155,0.013819283,-0.0044149836,0.008208596,0.0035099548,-0.018799512,0.0016097685,-0.016149499,0.0082730455,-0.0077184737,0.015928065,0.02904823,0.010770509,0.0060212957,0.0093488265,-0.17980398,0.00065543456,-0.011120125,0.033616036,-0.007481401,0.010021384,0.010973058,-0.00649485,0.02938978,-0.0030190167,-0.008107349,-0.000856504,-0.0038022366,0.026663415,0.007923805,-0.024025096,0.00072986406,-0.01046087,0.00012605388,-0.015031406,-0.031076614,-0.00874734,-0.014580476,0.011818738,0.008469983,0.007615456,-0.00