af586e53-b5fe-4658-88aa-ec6bc06ea251	[Context: complications > diabetic_retinopathy | ada]\nWhat You Need to Know About Diabetes and Your Eyes\n\nWhen your blood glucose (blood sugar) levels are above target range, over time, this can lead to diabetes-related eye disease. Diabetes affects your blood vessels, including the blood vessels in your eyes. As the blood vessels in the back of your eye are weakened, they can start to leak, resulting in blurry or cloudy vision, which is called diabetes-related retinopathy. Diabetes-related eye disease can cause vision loss.\n\nDiabetes is the leading cause of blindness in people 18–64 years old—and there are often no obvious signs or symptoms.\n\nEye Health\n\nRoutine Eye Exams: The What, When, How and Why\n\nDo you know the importance of having an annual eye exam? We walk you through the process of eye exams and the importance of maintaining eye health when living with diabetes.\n\nDiabetes & Your Eyes: Getting Started\n\nThe most important thing you can do to protect your eye health is scheduling a diabetes eye exam. These eye exams can help identify existing eye disease so you can take steps to prevent or delay vision loss caused by diabetes. Learn about the importance of a diabetes eye exam, what to expect, and how often you need an eye exam.\n\nDiabetes-related eye disease is the number one cause of blindness for working age Americans. Sadly, early diabetes-related eye disease often occurs before your vision is affected or you notice symptoms. Learn about the five major diabetes-related eye diseases.\n\nTaking care of your eyes is important—and getting them checked is an important step. However, there are additional things you can do to be proactive about protecting your vision.\n\nCalculate Your Risk for Diabetes-Related Retinopathy\n\nVision loss due to diabetes can be prevented with early detection, timely treatment, and preventive lifestyle changes. With this free RetinaRisk™ calculator, you can better understand the risk factors, calculate your risk, and learn simple steps you can take to prevent vision loss.\n\nBefore people develop type 2 diabetes, they almost always have prediabetes. There are no clear symptoms of prediabetes, so someone may have it and not even know it.\n\nOur champions have made the choice to prioritize their eye health and diabetes management. While championing their own health, they champion the health of others through their inspirational stories of learning to thrive despite their circumstances.\n\nRead these frequently asked questions to better understand the connection between diabetes and eye health.\n\nHow does diabetes affect vision?	{"url": "https://diabetes.org/health-wellness/eye-health", "title": "Diabetic Retinopathy", "topic": "diabetic_retinopathy", "source": "American Diabetes Association", "category": "complications", "file_path": "complications/diabetic_retinopathy/clean/ada/v1.md", "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "ada", "parent_document_id": "a82a3481-d346-4ba6-9e77-cd09be33f95e"}	[0.011431756,-0.013214403,-0.012894429,-0.056778777,-0.023771806,-0.005120511,0.0015021136,2.8577959e-05,0.016070273,0.011021454,-0.028466713,0.02556283,0.004177465,0.012392163,0.12320428,0.028444808,0.014613454,-0.011158953,0.001184442,0.0043921485,0.00706168,-0.0075917956,0.016174106,-0.008466941,-0.0011636718,-0.023959689,0.0089703,0.012932635,0.04849584,0.018952202,0.023575362,0.0027574403,0.027057063,0.013083566,0.013628061,0.019857125,-0.021366633,-0.026788,0.027814357,0.008069243,-0.0016861417,-0.014705937,0.012663306,-0.008749828,0.0011232416,-0.0112149315,0.004030916,-0.0039116717,0.006607514,0.021568896,-0.01524326,-0.005051201,-0.028598301,-0.17570463,0.009640596,-0.018387318,0.008150248,-0.009792043,0.0010758744,-0.0029931348,0.006827585,0.024153966,-0.0051510986,-0.023035493,-0.017738175,-0.0452607,0.011369524,-0.026805753,-0.024901541,0.0010347572,0.014515045,0.0005069523,-0.008988464,-0.0062107244,-0.016118221,-0.0043111