2f0dc400-c883-43eb-9387-f52dc672232f	[Context: complications > foot_care | cdc]\nLoss of hair on your toes, feet, and lower legs.\nDry, cracked skin on your feet.\nA change in the color and temperature of your feet.\nThickened, yellow toenails.\nFungus infections such as athlete's foot between your toes.\nA blister, sore, ulcer, infected corn, or ingrown toenail.\n\nMost people with diabetes can prevent serious foot complications. Regular care at home and going to all doctor's appointments are your best bet. Doing both will help you prevent foot problems (and stop small problems from becoming serious ones).	{"url": "https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/diabetes-complications/diabetes-and-your-feet.html", "title": "Diabetic Foot Care", "topic": "foot_care", "source": "Centers for Disease Control and Prevention", "category": "complications", "file_path": "complications/foot_care/clean/cdc/v1.md", "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "cdc", "parent_document_id": "06a4d5e3-0a28-40cc-a9c9-54d75af24ded"}	[0.0329688,0.0138482945,0.0069525014,-0.0077877487,0.0061096903,-0.00046963134,0.023820587,0.012155252,0.010721829,0.028084643,-0.025777433,-0.015231031,0.009675398,-0.0005412045,0.1180696,0.01251346,0.019437086,-0.005578671,0.013882523,0.008447125,-0.011483463,0.0045880172,-0.0110545,-0.010420538,0.028096644,-0.023661822,0.007927587,0.016492123,0.030637965,0.011845928,-0.006552573,0.0070581078,0.0056093098,-0.009111321,0.0081690755,0.004830237,0.008662408,-0.014960255,0.033015955,0.017096335,-0.024075534,0.024397293,-0.0054881847,0.0071969917,-0.0060750884,0.012413812,0.0072089927,0.022309134,0.019949399,0.019277604,-0.013553779,0.021193862,-0.005078087,-0.19768171,0.0055179517,-0.027631516,-0.012358664,0.0137654785,-0.002742866,0.008639422,-0.02343068,0.046987023,-0.015832888,-0.008859514,-0.0063661137,-0.038065128,0.020287503,-0.0031367342,-0.042643316,-0.0001613546,0.017132998,-0.004758487,-0.006926089,0.0022689495,-0.002731174,-0.010298683,-0.0045978734,0.