e8605fcd-475b-4643-bdf7-514c0c59f7a5	[Context: diagnosis > glucose_monitoring | cdc]\nYou'll fast (not eat) overnight before the test and have your blood drawn to measure your fasting blood sugar level. Then you'll drink the liquid and have your blood sugar level checked. These checks usually happen at 1 hour, 2 hours, and possibly 3 hours afterward.\n\nResults can differ depending on the size of the glucose drink and how often your blood sugar is tested. Ask your doctor what your test results mean.\n\nAfter a diagnosis\n\nIf your results show you have type 1, type 2, or gestational diabetes, talk with your doctor about a detailed treatment plan. Your plan should include a referral to:\n\nDiabetes self-management education and support services.\nAn endocrinologist (a doctor who diagnoses and treats hormone-related conditions). In its early stages, type 1 diabetes can be treated to avoid or delay symptoms and serious complications.\nA registered dietitian.\n\nYou'll also find out about specific steps you can take to be your healthiest no matter what type of diabetes you have.	{"url": "https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/diabetes-testing/index.html", "title": "Blood Glucose Monitoring", "topic": "glucose_monitoring", "source": "Centers for Disease Control and Prevention", "category": "diagnosis", "file_path": "diagnosis/glucose_monitoring/clean/cdc/v1.md", "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "cdc", "parent_document_id": "45ca5f3f-0ee5-4b6b-8b36-a16629707f85"}	[0.029896785,-0.032357957,-0.02352746,-0.03860159,0.02070499,-0.0112386495,0.014161015,0.017803377,0.016645836,0.0010192908,0.0007800511,-0.009749626,-0.0054204534,-0.0064768866,0.1252953,0.011693502,0.026783898,-0.0041898326,0.008689011,0.024267366,-0.013608115,0.0074500684,0.012882317,-0.0074063432,0.02998777,-0.022446185,0.015821746,0.0019229867,0.07039592,0.030031858,0.007063337,0.00934449,0.018144643,0.0076424815,0.007880501,0.009761297,-0.0065963003,-0.022320047,-0.009116199,-0.020820245,-0.000