df77e9d1-c99a-4111-ae1b-9df12943535a	[Context: diagnosis > random_blood_glucose | mayo]\nThis planning allows high doses of radiation to be delivered to the cancer while lowering the amount of radiation that reaches healthy tissue.\n\nWhat you can expect\n\nIntraoperative radiation therapy, also called IORT, happens during surgery. Many people who get IORT also have standard radiation therapy before surgery. Then during surgery, IORT is used to deliver a higher dose of radiation directly to the cancer than is possible with standard radiation therapy. Based on the treatment planning, radiation therapy delivered with IORT is carefully focused on the specific area that needs treatment.\n\nResults\n\nAfter intraoperative radiation therapy, you may have follow-up appointments to monitor the results. These appointments may include imaging tests to check if the cancer is gone. Talk with your healthcare team about your follow-up care.\n\nClinical trials\n\nExplore Mayo Clinic studies of tests and procedures to help prevent, detect, treat or manage conditions.	{"url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/blood-sugar-test/about/pac-20385150", "title": "Random Blood Sugar", "topic": "random_blood_glucose", "source": "Mayo Clinic", "category": "diagnosis", "file_path": "diagnosis/random_blood_glucose/clean/mayo/v1.md", "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 2, "source_org_code": "mayo", "parent_document_id": "e52cf8ee-12a6-42e3-9c35-6f0cdf56bcbf"}	[0.041105773,0.0018646441,-0.00564584,-0.06712254,0.0017382352,-0.004515662,-0.011986196,0.02963557,-0.0009863339,3.85782e-05,-0.008379879,0.0056334287,-0.01857178,-0.0032845838,0.12410759,0.028910745,0.00047144253,-0.009526021,0.008947313,0.004641852,0.00035555867,-0.022423964,0.0032032656,-0.017045064,0.001967887,-0.010366862,0.0042783045,0.022508537,0.056458894,0.0011517381,-0.009937387,-0.02079702,0.02041287,0.007356804,0.0026221885,0.036338873,-0.0039804834,-0.008136544,-0.027570905,-0.00071512576,-0.02055722,0.014805553,0.004