1a9e1792-6663-4d2c-a0ac-0a1ac362dd78	[Context: kidney > albumin_creatinine_ratio | ada]\nWhen you’re actively preventing diabetes-related kidney problems, it’s important to keep your body strong.\n\nDiscover new ways to be smarter about food with Diabetes Food Hub®. Find kidney-friendly recipes, a personalized grocery list, and plan meals to make sure everything you eat is helping to keep your kidneys healthy.\n\nFinding out you have kidney disease can be difficult to process. But making the right choices now can help you delay further kidney problems while letting you do what you love most.\n\nThere are things you can do that may help slow down kidney disease. Start by managing diabetes and making your life easier at the same time. Learn quick, easy ways to simplify your daily routine.\n\nImage\n\nRefill Meds Better\n\nMost insurance companies cover a 90-day supply of medication. That means fewer trips to the pharmacy. Talk with your pharmacist to coordinate your meds to refill them all at once.\n\nImage\n\nStay Organized\n\nKeep medical information and supplies in one place for easy access. Having all these important materials in one place makes it easier to prep for doctor’s visits and reordering supplies.\n\nImage\n\nShop for Food Online\n\nWhether you want to have groceries delivered or want to pick them up, shopping online can help limit impulse purchases. And it can help make sure you have all the healthy foods you need.\n\nImage\n\nWalk in the Morning\n\nFewer people are outside in the mornings, making it a great time for a relaxing workout and to start your day off right. Morning walks can improve memory and cognition in older adults.\n\nImage\n\nLate-Stage Kidney Disease\n\nStage 4 or stage 5 of chronic kidney disease means the kidneys are losing more of their function. Get helpful information on how to manage late-stage kidney disease.\n\nHere is some expert advice from nephrologists that can help you manage advanced CKD along with five things to discuss with your doctor.\n\nWhen kidney function declines too much, different health choices need to be made. Learn what happens during ESKD so you can manage your symptoms and find the right treatment.\n\nHome dialysis comes in two different forms, peritoneal dialysis and home hemodialysis. Both options offer freedom and flexibility by doing treatment in the comfort of your home.\n\nImage\n\nIn-Center Hemodialysis\n\nDialysis centers provide hemodialysis treatments by trained professionals. Many people choose in-center dialysis for the peace of mind of a clinic setting.\n\nImage\n\nSkilled Nursing Facility	{"url": "https://diabetes.org/health-wellness/kidney-care", "title": "Albumin-to-Creatinine Ratio (ACR)", "topic": "albumin_creatinine_ratio", "source": "American Diabetes Association", "category": "kidney", "file_path": "kidney/albumin_creatinine_ratio/clean/ada/v1.md", "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "ada", "parent_document_id": "d8a41cbd-0b25-4fe5-8294-56439be076d1"}	[0.02336386,-0.003858898,0.0037803536,-0.05470717,0.00022641534,-0.001373061,0.032366112,0.040779278,0.012146666,0.0052923937,-0.02961975,-0.011153438,0.012299073,0.018004,0.12390875,0.008695966,0.004563447,0.017687712,0.0111639835,-0.017666116,-0.0026106725,-0.0012391953,0.011402929,-0.0050619743,0.019579738,-0.020604871,0.031504516,0.02092581,0.024518548,0.026111942,0.0070938286,0.010937975,0.026464235,0.01952068,0.027656756,0.015722372,0.01057183,-0.033751838,0.01098207,0.006516802,-0.0057111694,0.006410608,0.012312198,0.00328871,0.009512041,-0.00972457,0.00010174917,0.007626001,0.03108977,0.036723413,0.034479413,0.009170593,-0.02946734,-0.16461843,0.01911413,-0.022494948,-0.01420976,0.0032738626,-0.005912684,0.016339371,-0.02761724,0.031624053,-0.027217373,-0.012424822,0.01015207,-0.023703692,0.019488087,-0.0130405035,-0.017177518,-0.022036582,-0.0018340644,-0.012873627,-0.015977478,-0.0095174685,-0.016770164,-0.017670639,-0.009124815,0.029191148,-0.015659193,0.015547166,0.003