31b978b1-ec43-4d62-9001-ac9f6b8a3418	[Context: kidney > bun | mayo]\nFor adult men, less than 17 mg/g.\nFor adult women, less than 25 mg/g.\n\nA higher than typical result may be a sign of kidney disease. The result may mean that diabetes has damaged the kidneys and led to a condition called diabetic nephropathy. This also is known as diabetic kidney disease.\n\nYour healthcare professional talks with you about the results of a creatinine test. Ask what the results mean for your health or treatment plan.\n\nClinical trials\n\nExplore Mayo Clinic studies of tests and procedures to help prevent, detect, treat or manage conditions.	{"url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/creatinine-test/about/pac-20384646", "title": "BUN (Blood Urea Nitrogen)", "topic": "bun", "source": "Mayo Clinic", "category": "kidney", "file_path": "kidney/bun/clean/mayo/v2.md", "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "mayo", "parent_document_id": "eb0cebb7-e5c5-4f15-b925-37b57b79f5b0"}	[0.009372603,0.0013630172,-0.022984719,-0.042871747,0.014877945,-0.012946951,0.022439977,0.031538703,0.01825333,0.0097208405,-0.00834978,0.0045392364,-0.013644289,-0.018348986,0.10921931,0.035412244,-0.006074388,0.015959607,0.0004377209,-0.0077863927,-0.01786735,0.006437389,0.00987128,0.0072734496,-0.0019831203,-0.013930064,-0.00087889784,0.017988626,0.029959584,0.02184715,0.0045744875,-0.034038465,0.019268086,0.021264983,0.011544177,0.03622959,0.0198817,-0.011647113,-0.021877313,-0.0017816597,-0.0062803766,0.008710603,-0.0062720627,0.020722954,0.017305866,0.00059535704,-0.023373205,0.007677323,0.024788242,0.040106386,-0.011159973,0.0024072414,-0.020634525,-0.17566355,0.005159326,-0.021098442,-0.010341562,0.027989786,0.01441076,0.013920101,-0.041773282,0.0060529043,-0.0070225475,-0.04187213,-0.017108522,-0.01793469,0.014433777,0.0034644764,-0.055539418,-0.019544415,-0.022346526,-0.00093966955,-0.010617682,0.008573383,-0.031664964,-0.007717949,-0.0030645547,0.019815927,0.0030372057,0.0094