67d07ad6-93e1-4b99-96c7-13ba4a0b1929	[Context: lifestyle > healthy_eating | cdc]\nKey points\n\nManaging blood sugar is the key to living well with diabetes, and healthy eating is the key to managing blood sugar.\nSimply put, eat healthy foods in the right amounts at the right times so your blood sugar stays in your target range as much as possible.\nWork with your dietitian or diabetes educator to create a healthy eating plan and check out these resources to learn more.\n\nEating well with diabetes\n\nDiscover helpful tools like the plate method and carb counting and learn about portion sizes.\n\nHere’s how counting carbs can help people with diabetes manage their blood sugar levels.\n\nFind out how many carbs are contained in common foods.\n\nHere's how to enjoy a meal out while sticking to your healthy eating plan.\n\nThese tips can help people with diabetes plan ahead to enjoy sweets and manage their blood sugar.\n\nEnjoying the holidays doesn’t mean you have to have mean a setback in your diabetes goals.\n\nFind out how you can embrace your culture when creating your diabetes meal plan.\n\nCancer treatment can disrupt your diabetes eating plan. Find tips to help manage both conditions.\n\nHelp for figuring out what to eat if you have diabetes and kidney disease.\n\nFiber can help you manage diabetes. Learn more about the surprising role of fiber.\n\nFood insecurity could increase your risk of developing type 2 diabetes or make it harder to manage.\n\nThese tips can help people with diabetes eat healthy on a budget.\n\nProvides tips for healthier eating at buffets for people with diabetes\n\nFind out how to choose the most nutritious carbs if you’re living with diabetes.\n\nDo you know how to spot hidden sugars in your everyday foods?	{"url": "https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/healthy-eating/index.html", "title": "Healthy Eating for Diabetes", "topic": "healthy_eating", "source": "Centers for Disease Control and Prevention", "category": "lifestyle", "file_path": "lif