6799576e-2f1f-41e9-bc27-5ce9ab3b6130	[Context: kidney > uric_acid | medlineplus]\nWhat is a uric acid test?\n\nA uric acid test measures the amount of uric acid in a sample of your blood or urine (pee). Uric acid is a normal waste product that your body makes when it breaks down chemicals called purines. These chemicals come from your cells when they die and can be found in certain foods and beverages.Â\n\nNormally, uric acid dissolves in your blood and is filtered out by the kidneys. It then exits your body through your urine. But if your body makes too much uric acid or your kidneys don't remove enough of it, uric acid can build up in your blood. When that happens, it can form needle-shaped crystals in and around your joints. This condition is called gout.Â\n\nGout is a type of arthritisÂ that causes painful swelling in your joints. High uric acid levels can also cause kidney stones, or kidney failure. But not everyone with high levels of uric acid will have these problems.\n\nOther names: serum urate, UA, uric acid: serum and urineÂ\n\nWhat is it used for?\n\nA uric acid test can be done using a blood or urine sample.\n\nAuric acid blood test may be used to:\n\nHelp diagnose gout, usually when done with a synovial fluid analysis. Synovial fluid helps keep your joints lubricated.\n\nMonitor uric acid levels in people who are having cancer chemotherapy or certain other cancer treatments. When treatment kills cancer cells quickly, they release large amounts of purines into the blood. This can lead to serious problems from high uric acid levels. Testing helps catch an increase in uric acid so it can be treated early.\n\nA uric acid urine test may be used to:\n\nHelp find out whether high levels of uric acid are causing kidney stones\n\nMonitor the risk of developing kidney stones in people who have gout\n\nWhy do I need a uric acid test?\n\nYou may need a uric acid blood test if you have symptoms of gout or another condition related to abnormal uric acid levels.\n\nSymptoms of gout usually occur in one joint at a time. The big toe is most commonly affected, but your other toes, ankles, or knees may also have symptoms. These can include:\n\nIntense pain\nSwelling, redness, and/or warmness around the joint\nLimited range of motion\n\nYou may also need this test if you:	{"url": "https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/uric-acid-test/", "title": "Uric Acid", "topic": "uric_acid", "source": "MedlinePlus", "category": "kidney", "file_path": "kidney/uric_acid/clean/medlineplus/v1.md", "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 5, "source_org_code": "medlineplus", "parent_document_id": "b7d8fd6d-24a7-42cc-b83f-63d165b5a06b"}	[0.045619152,0.008420957,0.026329437,-0.04776809,0.009087731,-0.006933252,-0.0035944514,0.031306602,-0.0142036,0.014373053,-0.011251041,-0.011138031,-0.024671346,-0.02295414,0.1044564,0.0009219324,-0.0063726837,-0.015219519,0.0060986783,-0.025582036,-0.0030464474,0.0025027369,0.016740512,0.015124927,-0.008102189,-0.0041362457,0.002240813,-0.015160211,0.054126263,0.010788746,-0.0041209226,-0.03581538,-0.011828666,0.021283599,0.013552112,0.013098439,-0.00433395,-0.009463813,-0.0035253353,0.0026722518,-0.01587912,0.018376153,-0.012326407,0.0042302827,0.0063159415,0.006484162,-0.025691774,-0.008844185,0.0141069535,-0.0006717009,0.0052726595,0.023440966,-0.009227718,-0.19726612,-0.015643429,-0.007759999,0.013285086,0.007163858,-0.005730933,0.0012576941,-0.016300919,-0.00047837337,-0.0064293286,-0.018880688,-0.01434461,-0.03251122,-0.00018969018,-0.00965567,-0.03851792,-0.03843268,0.0039917952,0.016446883,0.00013681847,-0.0017188202,-0.038430214,-0.009468189,0.017018426,0.01638978,0.00048094554,0.013201965,-0.005866214,-0.015835932,-0.006290844,-0.03242536,0.0038344832,0.011681195,-0.00931407,0.02331387,-0.012839527,0.011510767,-0.0017790312,0.0028014097,0.044994984,0.0048460728,0.01565574,0.013928414,0.008271089,-0.02563934,-0.012071884,0.015714796,-0.028289346,0.019990725,-0.020678949,0.0071945176,-0.022652306,-0.0056548077,0.0113090