37dd1294-c91f-4d63-8add-a735c7234bdf	[Context: kidney > uric_acid | medlineplus]\nMany medicines, including aspirin, can affect uric acid levels in your blood and urine. Taking niacin (vitamin B-3) can also affect your results. So, be sure to tell your provider about all the medicines you take. But donât stop taking any medicines without talking with your provider first.\n\nAre there any risks to the test?\n\nThere is no known risk to having a uric acid blood or urine test.\n\nWhat do the results mean?\n\nHigh uric acid levels in a blood test may happen if your body makes too much uric acid or if your kidneys can't properly remove uric acid from your blood. You may also have high levels if youâre eating too many foods that are high in purines, such as:\n\nRed meat and organ meats, including liver and kidney\nCertain kinds of seafood, including shellfish, anchovies, sardines, trout, and tuna\nAlcohol (all types)\nHigh fructose corn syrup in soda and sweets\n\nYour provider may order more tests to help diagnose whatâs causing the problem. High levels of uric acid may be related to many conditions, including:\n\nGout\nKidney disease or kidney stones\nLeukemia, multiple myeloma, or cancer that has spread in your body (metastatic cancer)\nSide effects from certain cancer treatments, such as chemotherapy\n\nAlcohol use disorder\nPreeclampsia, a condition that can cause dangerously high blood pressure in pregnant women\n\nLow levels of uric acid in blood are uncommon and usually donât cause health problems. Health conditions that are related to low uric acid levels are usually diagnosed using other tests.\n\nHigh uric levels in urine, may be related to:\n\nGout\nKidney stones or having a high risk for kidney stones\nLeukemia, multiple myeloma, or cancer that has spread in your body\n\nObesity\nAn inherited genetic condition, such as Lesch-Nyhan syndrome, that makes it hard for your body to get rid of uric acid\n\nLow levels of uric acid in urine may be related to kidney disease, lead poisoning, or alcohol use disorder.Â\n\nIf your results show a high level of uric acid in your blood or urine, it doesn't always mean you have a condition that needs treatment. Many people have high levels of uric acid without having health problems.\n\nIf you have questions about your results, talk with your provider.	{"url": "https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/uric-acid-test/", "title": "Uric Acid", "topic": "uric_acid", "source": "MedlinePlus", "category": "kidney", "file_path": "kidney/uric_acid/clean/medlineplus/v1.md", "chunk_index": 2, "total_chunks": 5, "source_org_code": "medlineplus", "parent_document_id": "b7d8fd6d-24a7-42cc-b83f-63d165b5a06b"}	[0.040185016,-0.0039085755,0.013222884,-0.066242635,0.014531685,-0.017639747,0.0031445678,0.040984057,0.008567744,0.009009996,0.00580593,-0.016085135,-0.011957464,-0.017283095,0.10705289,-0.006886899,0.0048656366,-0.019792745,0.008354435,-0.010066909,0.010124023,-0.0014300073,0.010719266,0.010976597,-0.001965602,0.007828268,-0.015405673,-0.030527746,0.040811922,0.018869543,8.603088e-05,-0.03664989,-0.004648579,0.017818378,0.020978494,0.023555288,-0.009162242,-0.011046931,0.0012407567,-0.015837472,0.002658464,0.004303001,-0.03289295,0.0049456744,0.016158199,0.0041799624,-0.005594827,-0.0043534487,0.034669247,-0.006447575,0.004760121,0.013839585,-0.0073698033,-0.19761756,0.0085015865,-0.00849778,0.026278324,0.002825321,-0.008627721,-0.00822043,-0.016892577,0.01830086,0.006029018,-0.042347975,-0.017218845,-0.04232955,0.027084216,-0.0028331683,-0.028935008,-0.041222937,-0.0036622672,0.00048218985,-0.00893323,-0.0024460775,-0.015643103,-0.005514932,0.0045585684,0.031287156,-0.005352189,-0.01726713,-0.006205577,-0.030225823,-0.012065462,-0.030867338,0.0123327775,0.022483064,-0.0020345838,-0.007926932,-0.013221446,0.016066624,0.011768478,0.021470545,0.030647215,0.0005611099,0.005464484,0.014296732,0.02469761,-0.017884295,-0.005710443,0.020750817,-0.008080703,0.01853122,-0.023510708,0.0028974507,-0.021246668,0.0