7993d6f1-2b0a-477b-bf61-1269c6f8718d	[Context: lipid > hdl | medlineplus]\nHigh levels of triglycerides may increase the risk of heart disease, especially in women.\n\nThere is another type of cholesterol called VLDLÂ (very low-density lipoprotein). Some people also call VLDL a "bad" cholesterol because it contributes to the buildup of plaque in your arteries. But VLDL and LDL are different; VLDL mainly carries triglycerides, and LDL mainly carries cholesterol. VLDL isn't usually included in routine cholesterol tests because it's difficult to measure. Because VLDL contains a certain percentage of triglycerides, a lab can use your triglycerides level to estimate your VLDL level.\n\nWhy do I need a cholesterol test?\n\nYour provider may order a cholesterol test as part of a routine exam. When and how often you should get a cholesterol test depends on your age, risk factors, and family history. The general recommendations are:\n\nFor people who are age 19 or younger:\n\nThe first test should be between ages 9 to 11\nChildren should have the test again every 5 years\nSome children may have this test starting at age 2 if there is a family history of high cholesterol, heart attack, or stroke\n\nFor people who are ages 20 to 65:\n\nYounger adults should have the test every 5 years\nMen ages 45 to 65 and women ages 55 to 65 should have it every 1 to 2 years\n\nFor people older than 65:\n\nThey should be tested every year\n\nYou may also have a cholesterol test more often if you are at high risk of heart problems because of:\n\nA family history of heart disease\n\nHigh blood pressure\n\nType 2 diabetes\n\nSmoking\nExcess weight or obesity\n\nLack of physical activity\nA diet high in saturated fat\n\nWhat happens during a cholesterol test?\n\nA health care professional will take a blood sample from a vein in your arm, using a small needle. After the needle is inserted, a small amount of blood will be collected into a test tube or vial. You may feel a little sting when the needle goes in or out. This usually takes less than five minutes.\n\nYou may be able to use an at-home kitÂ to check your cholesterol levels. Your kit will include a device to prick your finger to collect a drop of blood for testing. Be sure to follow the kit instructions carefully.	{"url": "https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/cholesterol-levels/", "title": "HDL Cholesterol", "topic": "hdl", "source": "MedlinePlus", "category": "lipid", "file_path": "lipid/hdl/clean/medlineplus/v1.md", "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 8, "source_org_code": "medlineplus", "parent_document_id": "870a3b19-a32e-4e8c-8b2f-cb8599fd9894"}	[-0.00067295914,-0.006048757,1.0224719e-05,-0.060847726,0.009752771,-0.018131373,0.013768309,0.037566975,0.0069216657,-0.008488532,0.012463071,0.013632234,-0.0065725893,-0.0067552724,0.110397555,0.025940973,0.016593246,-0.008554853,-0.0072487723,-0.012082235,0.010684769,0.018255593,0.008124611,-0.008992883,-0.010744542,-0.011944885,0.0073817787,0.0007486905,0.036843847,0.019347986,0.004644886,-0.034608547,0.011918068,0.015967434,0.01054025,0.02013375,0.0015540849,-0.006142946,0.0014122423,0.008883621,0.0020438912,-0.00016484296,-0.020699631,-0.004373416,0.030699665,-0.016036797,-0.017348722,-0.00811646,0.02333369,0.009033721,0.0008705955,0.014376288,-0.017247705,-0.18380678,0.014940777,0.0048382226,-0.01088173,-0.029952206,0.00795501,-0.009608238,-0.033902824,-0.0018738055,-0.013597155,-0.01531905,-0.014140572,-0.026509311,0.021883849,0.002457523,-0.027725793,-0.008165438,0.022838999,0.043201413,0.005633773,-0.014853174,-0.019967886,-0.02688199,-0.01853481,-0.00240327,-0.0063154143,-0.00307181,-0.022137307,-0.0017344382,0.0032760222,-0.026166596,-0.0042305193,0.0041480907,-0.0042002928,-0.011193432,-0.010955535,0.010969468,-0.0053521357,0.020709408,0.021293381,0.021837119,-0.0047071483,0.021455474,0.023825755,-0.010648784,0.0007594493,-0.0015547925,-0.0052110595,-0.011357752,0.008364342,-0.014043074,-0.0032321485,0.006422349,0.009036203,0.01756818,0.021316445