1881e476-e278-41f2-8e07-56fa68ebe46f	[Context: lipid > ldl | medlineplus]\nHigh levels of triglycerides may increase the risk of heart disease, especially in women.\n\nThere is another type of cholesterol called VLDLÂ (very low-density lipoprotein). Some people also call VLDL a "bad" cholesterol because it contributes to the buildup of plaque in your arteries. But VLDL and LDL are different; VLDL mainly carries triglycerides, and LDL mainly carries cholesterol. VLDL isn't usually included in routine cholesterol tests because it's difficult to measure. Because VLDL contains a certain percentage of triglycerides, a lab can use your triglycerides level to estimate your VLDL level.\n\nWhy do I need a cholesterol test?\n\nYour provider may order a cholesterol test as part of a routine exam. When and how often you should get a cholesterol test depends on your age, risk factors, and family history. The general recommendations are:\n\nFor people who are age 19 or younger:\n\nThe first test should be between ages 9 to 11\nChildren should have the test again every 5 years\nSome children may have this test starting at age 2 if there is a family history of high cholesterol, heart attack, or stroke\n\nFor people who are ages 20 to 65:\n\nYounger adults should have the test every 5 years\nMen ages 45 to 65 and women ages 55 to 65 should have it every 1 to 2 years\n\nFor people older than 65:\n\nThey should be tested every year\n\nYou may also have a cholesterol test more often if you are at high risk of heart problems because of:\n\nA family history of heart disease\n\nHigh blood pressure\n\nType 2 diabetes\n\nSmoking\nExcess weight or obesity\n\nLack of physical activity\nA diet high in saturated fat\n\nWhat happens during a cholesterol test?\n\nA health care professional will take a blood sample from a vein in your arm, using a small needle. After the needle is inserted, a small amount of blood will be collected into a test tube or vial. You may feel a little sting when the needle goes in or out. This usually takes less than five minutes.\n\nYou may be able to use an at-home kitÂ to check your cholesterol levels. Your kit will include a device to prick your finger to collect a drop of blood for testing. Be sure to follow the kit instructions carefully.	{"url": "https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/cholesterol-levels/", "title": "LDL Cholesterol", "topic": "ldl", "source": "MedlinePlus", "category": "lipid", "file_path": "lipid/ldl/clean/medlineplus/v1.md", "chunk_index": 1, "total_chunks": 8, "source_org_code": "medlineplus", "parent_document_id": "cc5a815c-6cf3-4cca-92bd-f9014c0927ac"}	[-0.0005694758,-0.005143341,-0.0021393301,-0.061155066,0.008688294,-0.014097342,0.012553881,0.037959937,0.006429246,-0.0082073435,0.011752962,0.011227394,-0.0051995483,-0.0082730455,0.109672084,0.022853592,0.019258533,-0.009012091,-0.0064693596,-0.015502673,0.010365582,0.015596997,0.007227907,-0.006828778,-0.01180699,-0.005801841,0.007223269,0.0010636006,0.036745045,0.02317034,0.0049226703,-0.034377884,0.012961968,0.014951738,0.009084538,0.019639833,-0.00092293834,-0.0075316294,0.00033580902,0.007500703,0.0027257511,-0.0014097074,-0.019858973,-0.007213644,0.029093437,-0.016482389,-0.018127948,-0.0058458014,0.019359237,0.0099950135,-0.0037177438,0.010355632,-0.015195157,-0.18456367,0.014034128,0.0015647771,-0.013610638,-0.028811844,0.0091735935,-0.011742433,-0.035321206,-0.0013262487,-0.013032691,-0.013367148,-0.013534336,-0.024971444,0.023149941,-0.0006581812,-0.027105803,-0.00899397,0.02215586,0.043604024,0.0060854037,-0.018186769,-0.020917088,-0.028018134,-0.020576818,0.001835269,-0.007436837,-0.00046189033,-0.0217769,-0.0038715603,0.00452263,-0.02482865,-0.006279348,0.007306069,-0.001259801,-0.011723663,-0.011476762,0.011114312,-0.0066032712,0.019532776,0.021728218,0.025140466,-0.0045880224,0.02342247,0.026193336,-0.011149454,0.0023337551,-0.0021513284,-0.004736841,-0.008990023,0.0073536457,-0.010575662,-0.0030884824,0.00456343,0.009932368,0.020361528,0.02