cf7722ac-7d93-430e-af11-0597c2a77d78	[Context: liver > fatty_liver | cleveland]\nYour liver plays a key role in your health. It has hundreds of important jobs. When too much fat begins to build up (steatosis), it affects how well your liver works. Some types of steatotic (fatty) liver disease are mild, while others can become more serious. Early care can help prevent long-term damage.\n\nAdvertisement\n\nCleveland Clinic is a non-profit academic medical center. Advertising on our site helps support our mission. We do not endorse non-Cleveland Clinic products or services. Policy\n\nImage content: This image is available to view online.\n\nView image online (https://my.clevelandclinic.org/-/scassets/Images/org/health/articles/15831-fatty-liver-disease.jpg)\n\nSteatotic liver disease (SLD), formerly called fatty liver disease, happens when too much fat builds up in your liver. It’s one of the most common types of liver disease. Many people don’t know they have it at first. It often doesn’t cause symptoms in the early stages.\n\nOver time, extra fat in your liver can lead to inflammation and damage. In some people, this damage gets worse and causes scarring. Severe scarring can affect how well your liver works and lead to serious health problems.\n\nMany conditions cause steatosis of the liver. Steatosis is often reversible, especially in the early stages and before cirrhosis develops. Treatment often focuses on managing underlying conditions. Your healthcare provider may also recommend making changes to your daily habits.\n\n“Steatotic liver disease” is an umbrella term. It includes several types:\n\nWhile each type has different causes, they all involve fat buildup in the liver.\n\nEarly on, steatotic (fatty) liver disease often doesn’t cause symptoms. When symptoms do occur, they may include:\n\nAs the disease gets worse, symptoms may include:\n\nThe main cause of steatotic (fatty) liver disease is fat buildup in your liver. This can happen for different reasons, depending on the type.\n\nCommon causes include:\n\nYou may be more likely to develop steatotic liver disease if you:\n\nThe best way to prevent steatotic liver disease is to maintain your overall health. You can do this by:\n\nIf you have risk factors, like Type 2 diabetes or obesity, regular checkups can help catch problems early.\n\nWithout treatment, damage can gradually build up in your liver. The stages of steatotic (fatty) liver disease are:	{"url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/15831-fatty-liver-disease", "title": "Fatty Liver Disease", "topic": "fatty_liver", "source": "Cleveland Clinic", "category": "liver", "file_path": "liver/fatty_liver/clean/cleveland/v1.md", "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 2, "source_org_code": "cleveland", "parent_document_id": "76933a01-b019-46c0-8fa1-55e3d4e56350"}	[0.0114609115,-0.014261041,0.002316124,-0.044110414,0.012616581,0.00226855,0.005584411,0.02661043,0.027083281,0.025501575,-0.025517674,-0.0135280145,-0.0083973,-0.00945471,0.10948875,0.016891774,-0.003920772,0.00025357585,0.005316633,0.0066580656,0.01825871,0.00033762585,0.008941933,0.0027672322,-0.020246906,-0.014462222,0.026865505,-0.029966073,0.029269222,-0.014130224,0.018574279,-0.013899042,0.0056270994,0.008411544,0.025246872,0.014876411,0.0032759171,-0.014161303,0.0011482097,0.020782623,-0.009599119,0.0124556525,0.011329777,0.008923848,0.0051727523,0.020696042,0.035960857,0.010018935,0.020466322,-0.0046752295,-0.01043974,-0.018412542,-0.028849926,-0.17863472,0.0012167745,-0.012656028,0.00047432678,-0.024239575,0.016230004,-0.017409105,-0.015049182,0.042432845,-0.025964512,-0.015915774,0.013710471,-0.009498574,0.0005958067,-0.025633348,-0.010608276,-0.0041927667,0.017106315,0.0021249775,0.002756015,-0.016971657,-0.0047005033,-0.007811965,0.010793298,0.007070222,0.0025030356,0.022055207,-0.021106187,-0.008146821,-0.03781772,-0.023257583,0.030769866,0.024084957,0.002927319,-0.00045567146,0.010056241,0.010967901,0.007376832,0.033213273,0.014857038,0.01