08849b76-3a93-4e9d-b743-b20acba4499d	[Context: medications > thiazolidinediones | cleveland]\nPioglitazone is a medication that treats type 2 diabetes. It helps your body use insulin more effectively and decreases your blood sugar. A healthcare provider may recommend changes to your diet and exercise if you take this medication. The brand name of this medication is Actos®.\n\nAdvertisement\n\nCleveland Clinic is a non-profit academic medical center. Advertising on our site helps support our mission. We do not endorse non-Cleveland Clinic products or services. Policy\n\nPIOGLITAZONE (pye oh GLI ta zone) treats type 2 diabetes. It helps your body use insulin effectively, which decreases your blood sugar (glucose). Changes to diet and exercise are often combined with this medication.\n\nThis medicine may be used for other purposes; ask your health care provider or pharmacist if you have questions.\n\nCOMMON BRAND NAME(S): Actos\n\nThey need to know if you have any of these conditions:\n\nTake this medication by mouth with a glass of water. Follow the directions on the prescription label. Take your medication at the same time each day. Do not take more often than directed.\n\nA special MedGuide will be given to you by the pharmacist with each prescription and refill. Be sure to read this information carefully each time.\n\nTalk to your care team about the use of this medication in children. Special care may be needed.\n\nOverdosage: If you think you have taken too much of this medicine contact a poison control center or emergency room at once.\n\nNOTE: This medicine is only for you. Do not share this medicine with others.\n\nIf you miss a dose, take it as soon as you can. If it is almost time for your next dose, take only that dose. Do not take double or extra doses.\n\nOther medications may affect the way this medication works. Talk with your care team about all the medications you take. They may suggest changes to your treatment plan to lower the risk of side effects and to make sure your medications work as intended.\n\nSome medications may affect your blood sugar levels or hide the symptoms of low blood sugar (hypoglycemia). Talk with your care team about all the medications you take. They may suggest changes to your dose or checking your blood sugar levels more often.\n\nMedications that may affect your blood sugar levels include:\n\nMedications that may mask symptoms of low blood sugar include:\n\nThis list may not describe all possible interactions.	{"url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/drugs/19069-pioglitazone-tablets", "title": "Thiazolidinediones (TZDs)", "topic": "thiazolidinediones", "source": "Cleveland Clinic", "category": "medications", "file_path": "medications/thiazolidinediones/clean/cleveland/v1.md", "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 3, "source_org_code": "cleveland", "parent_document_id": "399c924f-7983-44dc-a5b2-aa9b5133814b"}	[0.033205237,-0.017635696,-0.015608144,-0.06594119,0.0011999505,-0.014323392,0.005509741,0.011740691,0.0178158,0.0010306631,-0.025769537,-0.01983904,-0.0004132104,-0.018599182,0.1249391,0.004498433,-0.01644692,0.001595825,0.011001507,-0.003277992,-0.00097238534,-0.0018883072,0.0048636408,-0.018045513,0.015895752,-0.017168382,0.0014089908,-0.00599449,0.03762343,0.0029920214,0.013687499,0.017504608,0.027777381,0.01921872,0.018382935,-0.011218264,0.03490632,0.0066035986,-0.02289443,0.0043618376,-0.014334259,0.022923313,-0.0130159445,0.03208264,-0.0022294072,0.0058679143,0.0032311266,-0.0009119621,0.034126032,0.0068638977,-0.0063465056,0.004435195,-0.03175154,-0.178645,-0.00049435353,-0.003157523,-0.005945461,-2.5269432e-05,-0.004122667,-0.008719784,0.012818222,0.012821445,0.0022672664,-0.008182859,-0.02717814,-0.021755133,0.01121957,-0.0257697,0.0090985345,-0.012845042,0.014634568,-0.011404035,-0.0032286493,-0.0015577009,-0.011533798,-0.01178294,0.0031176652,0.017370583,0.004511396,0.0029113612,-0.0231605,-0.01622164,-0.033925403,-0.019724095,0.015789744,-0.021116225,0.015191583,-0